  "answer_text": "The URL you provided (`mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx`) is an older, legacy web address for the **Georgia Department of Revenue (DOR) Motor Vehicle Division (MVD)**. \n\nGeorgia transitioned its vehicle services to a unified online platform called **Georgia DRIVES (Driver Record and Integrated Vehicle Enterprise System)**. \n\nTo renew your tags, order plates, or manage your vehicle registration, use the current official Georgia DMV channels:\n\n### 1. Official Georgia DRIVES Portal\nYou can complete almost all tag and title services online:\n* **Website:** **[eservices.drives.ga.gov](https://eservices.drives.ga.gov)**\n* **What you can do here:**\n  * Renew your vehicle registration (tags)\n  * Check the status of your vehicle title or registration\n  * Estimate your Title Ad Valorem Tax (TAVT)\n  * Change your registration address\n  * Cancel vehicle registration voluntarily (e.g., if you sell or store the car)\n  * Pay insurance fines\n  * Search and select specialty or prestige license plates\n\n### 2. Georgia MV Express Kiosks\nIf you need your tag immediately and do not want to wait for it to arrive in the mail, you can use a self-service kiosk. \n* **Where to find them:** Many Kroger and other select retail stores throughout Georgia house these kiosks.\n* **How they work:** You scan your renewal notice or enter your information, pay the fee, and the kiosk prints your new license plate decal right on the spot.\n* **Find a kiosk near you:** [Georgia MV Express Kiosk Locator](https://gamv_express.com/) *(Note: search for participating locations in your county)*.\n\n### 3. County Tag Office\nIf you have a complex registration issue or prefer to do your business in person, you can visit your local county tax commissioner's tag office. You can look up your specific county's location, hours, and contact details via the [Georgia Department of Revenue County Tag Office Finder](https://dor.georgia.gov/county-tag-offices).",
